{"text": " Welcome to Welcome to WhatsApp Business AI. I am so glad you are here. A Nairobi Property Agency was paying three customer service agents to answer the same 15 questions on WhatsApp every day, opening hours, property prices, viewing slots. A developer built a bot in a weekend. The bot now handles 340 conversations daily. The three agents moved to closing deals. Revenue went up 40% in 90 days. By the end of this course, you will set up a Metacloud API account and send your first WhatsApp message via code by Lesson 2. You will build a webhook server that receives and passes any incoming WhatsApp message type. You will build a complete FAQ bot that handles 10 question types including Swahili and English variations. You will integrate Claude or GPT as the AI Intelligence layer, freeform messages handled automatically. And you will. Deploy a production bot with full error handling, delivery tracking and full back to human logic. This course has eight lessons and six hours of content with five hands-on sandboxes. Your final project is production deployed customer service bot for Savannah Properties, a fictional Kenyan real estate company. You do not need to code, you do not need a technology background. All you need is the willingness to learn and I will guide you every step of the way. Your first task is waiting below. I will see you in Lesson 1. Your skills bear fruit.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 6.28, "text": " Welcome to Welcome to WhatsApp Business AI. I am so glad you are here.", "tokens": [50364, 4027, 281, 4027, 281, 30513, 10715, 7318, 13, 286, 669, 370, 5404, 291, 366, 510, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14923026643950363, "compression_ratio": 1.4357541899441342, "no_speech_prob": 0.01226507592946291, "words": [{"word": " Welcome", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.9241504669189453}, {"word": " to", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.8, "probability": 0.9797602295875549}, {"word": " Welcome", "start": 0.8